  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "3 v 3 – quick finishes",
  "description": "Play 3 v 3 in a small area, about 20 × 15 metres. Blue attack a big goal with a keeper, red attack two small goals at the other end. Play 3–4 minutes and rest 1 minute, four times. With more than six players, use substitutes.\n\nThe focus is daring to shoot and using wall passes to get a shot off. No fixed positions – everyone attacks and everyone defends. Swap so both teams get to attack the big goal.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Dare to shoot – every chance is a shooting chance."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Use a wall pass to get past a defender."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Few touches, and move before and after you have had the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If you lose the ball – work together and win it back straight away."
    }
  ],
